<article class="env-remark" id="0FDL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FDL">Remark <span data-tag="0FDL">36.38.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of locally Noetherian schemes. There is a map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_* : K'_0(X) \longrightarrow K'_0(Y)  \]
</div>
  <p> which sends $[\mathcal{F}]$ to </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [\bigoplus \nolimits _{i \geq 0} R^{2i}f_*\mathcal{F}] - [\bigoplus \nolimits _{i \geq 0} R^{2i + 1}f_*\mathcal{F}]  \]
</div>
  <p> This is well defined because the sheaves $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ are coherent (Cohomology of Schemes, Proposition <a href="/tag/02O5" data-tag="02O5">30.19.1</a>), because locally only a finite number are nonzero, and because a short exact sequence of coherent sheaves on $X$ produces a long exact sequence of $R^ if_*$ on $Y$. If $Y$ is quasi-compact (the only case most often used in practice), then we can rewrite the above as </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_*[\mathcal{F}] = \sum (-1)^ i[R^ if_*\mathcal{F}] = [Rf_*\mathcal{F}]  \]
</div>
  <p> where we have used the equality $K'_0(Y) = K_0(D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(Y))$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/0FDF" data-tag="0FDF">36.38.1</a>. </p>
</article>